From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:32:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: import bone mass, body water and BMR from Health
 Connect

A smart scale (Hume Body Pod via Samsung Health) can write more than the
weight / body fat / lean mass NOOP already imports. BoneMassRecord,
BodyWaterMassRecord and BasalMetabolicRateRecord now ride the Body
composition category (same consent, selection and grant gating) and land in
metricSeries under the Health Connect source as bone_mass (kg), body_water
(kg) and bmr (kcal/day), latest reading of each local day, keyed by the
record's own offset like upstream's weight. Nothing is written when Health
Connect holds none of them.

The importer also remembers the time of the newest scale reading (fork
prefs), since the stored series carry only a day. ScaleBody is the pure
snapshot model (newest values, ~7 / ~30 day deltas, 30-day weight trend)
the card and the coach line build on.

Hooks: one spread line in BODY_COMPOSITION, one read call before the
write-out, one append to the metricSeries batch, three manifest permissions.
All logic lives in ScaleImport.kt / ScaleBody.kt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
